  "layout_change": "2026-11-22: business modules flattened, intervention renamed gate, evaluation-only workflow separated; algorithm bodies unchanged by this layout migration.",
  "behavior_changes": {
    "session.py": "Requirement extraction is deduplicated by (user text, repository context); revised contracts receive ordered user messages. Default agent delivery uses an unbounded full Brief instead of a 6000-character projection.",
    "task_contract/extraction.py": "2026-11-24: remove character truncation of extracted goal, objective, symptom and reproduction text; requirement and constraint text remains complete. Shared extraction change also applies to evaluation. Preserve full Goal/objective/symptom/reproduction text and all fallback requirement entries.",
    "claims/maintenance.py": "2026-11-23: opt-in requirement reassessment with historical evidence. 2026-11-24: invalid current-contract conflict excerpts are discarded per row rather than rejecting the window; this validation change also affects independent evaluation. 2026-11-24: default Brief has no character budget and no automatic size/phase folding; explicit finite-budget evaluation callers retain folding. Unbounded default does not trigger size/count/phase Claim folding; explicit finite budgets retain folding.",
    "claims/store.py": "Replacing the task contract invalidates R/K coverage and R/K conflict notes.",
    "briefing/render.py": "2026-11-24: render existing Goal symptom entries as reported background, not current verified behavior or requirements. Full Brief shows bounded excerpts and a Goal inspection pointer; compact Brief shows a count and pointer. Shared renderer change also applies to independent evaluation, affects Brief text/budget, and is not claimed behavior-equivalent to upstream. 2026-11-24: failed-check focus follows merged child provenance and retains the original failure scope across unrelated later passes. Rendering and priority change also applies to independent evaluation; explicit stale/superseded claims still retire through the existing protocol. 2026-11-24: default Brief rendering is unbounded and preserves full Goal/R/K, active claims, reference IDs, tensions, symptoms, verification focus and read coverage. Explicit finite budgets retain the legacy bounded mode. Applies to product and any evaluation callers using defaults; no equivalence or benchmark improvement claimed. Unbounded default renders complete contract and active Claim text, references, symptoms, tensions, verification focus and read coverage. Explicit finite budgets retain the legacy evaluation path.",
    "evidence/observation.py": " 2026-11-24: populate missing action_input from actual supplied command/arguments at observation capture; preserve explicit input. Applies to both product and independent evaluation, with existing bounded evidence storage.",
    "briefing/evidence.py": "2026-11-24: max_files=None renders every tracked file and read range for complete Briefs; finite legacy evidence-context callers retain their limits. An explicit None file limit renders all recorded files and read ranges.",
    "claims/inspection.py": "2026-11-24: display the complete stored evidence excerpt in detail queries; evidence ingestion semantics unchanged. Detail queries return the full stored evidence excerpt."
  }
